    },
    {
      "position": 1,
      "source_id": null,
      "text": "FORMATION:\nＶ(dict. form/たform/ているform) + とおり(に)\nＮ + の + とおり(に)\nＮ + どおり(に)",
      "html": "FORMATION:<br/>Ｖ(dict. form/たform/ているform) + とおり(に)<br/>Ｎ + の + とおり(に)<br/>Ｎ + どおり(に)",
      "credits_raw": "rubyhatchet",
      "content_sha256": "039eecd29bd150e3ed1c20f36223a38cc1575cd2f6574bc1ace2f123dc3a77c9",
      "original_created_at": null,
      "original_updated_at": null
    },
    {
      "position": 2,
      "source_id": null,
      "text": "私が言った通りになったでしょう！\nwatashi ga itta _toori_ ni natta deshou!",
      "html": "私が言った通りになったでしょう！<br/>watashi ga itta _toori_ ni natta deshou!",
      "credits_raw": "Miki",
      "content_sha256": "7c6d2fda5a9f0f8a1be933d809c65ca01f81017eba5109c0cffd137aa488c0c1",
      "original_created_at": null,
      "original_updated_at": null
    },
    {
      "position": 3,
      "source_id": null,
      "text": "Formed from (plain) verb + toori or\nnoun + toori.\nNote that a euphonic change to doori is possible depending on what it follows.\n\nV = Verb\nN = Noun",
      "html": "Formed from (plain) verb + toori or<br/>noun + toori.<br/>Note that a euphonic change to doori is possible depending on what it follows.<br/><br/>V = Verb<br/>N = Noun",
      "credits_raw": "Amatuka",
      "content_sha256": "0d922c125e2667d7886ac06810fc4f29d83f02611475670b448966d170b50f9b",
      "original_created_at": null,
      "original_updated_at": null
    },
    {
      "position": 4,
      "source_id": null,
      "text": "when does it have に after?\n私が教えた通りに、、",
      "html": "when does it have に after?<br/>私が教えた通りに、、",
      "credits_raw": "dc",
      "content_sha256": "f6a18abbae484f98becbc9887da8b4b8348d819debe49167f6bb045929a171f6",
      "original_created_at": null,
      "original_updated_at": null
    },
    {
      "position": 5,
      "source_id": null,
      "text": "You can also say \n予想 通りに 日本チームが優勝した。\n彼女は もと 通りに 元気になった。",
      "html": "You can also say <br/>予想 通りに 日本チームが優勝した。<br/>彼女は もと 通りに 元気になった。",
      "credits_raw": "Miki",
      "content_sha256": "857b3830cd7b5a588a837bcb1ecd19f5aa7ca78fc3cefd30f3d5f664f89bd3cd",
      "original_created_at": null,
      "original_updated_at": null
    },
    {
      "position": 6,
      "source_id": null,
      "text": "The example is actually 'doori'. 予想通り 【よそうどおり】 (exp) as expected (neutral and negative events); as feared",
      "html": "The example is actually 'doori'. 予想通り 【よそうどおり】 (exp) as expected (neutral and negative events); as feared",
      "credits_raw": "Amatuka",
      "content_sha256": "1292c545a9d16c3f993e57218a1f3cc79e71d0b2c858a8f5bb8ec91356a6eca9",
      "original_created_at": null,
      "original_updated_at": null
    },
    {
      "position": 7,
      "source_id": null,
      "text": "Many '通り' 'toori' examples are actually a literal 'way' as in street.",
      "html": "Many '通り' 'toori' examples are actually a literal 'way' as in street.",
      "credits_raw": "Amatuka",
      "content_sha256": "1239ea69c71486c6fa8567b6141048f8d51078915f18a0200931f3798508238b",
      "original_created_at": null,
      "original_updated_at": null
    },
    {
      "position": 8,
      "source_id": null,
      "text": "chizu no toori ni mairimashta kara, zenzen mayoimasen deshta.",
      "html": "chizu no toori ni mairimashta kara, zenzen mayoimasen deshta.",
      "credits_raw": "prachi_saurabh",
      "content_sha256": "244da80f8feadc8b49ef7f4ae7ed67f9faeb41a463c51f49951bc4feccd88db1",
      "original_created_at": null,
      "original_updated_at": null
    },
    {
      "position": 9,
      "source_id": null,
      "text": "toori ni.... expreses the idea that something takes place in the same way as something... or it could be negative also.. means doesn't take place..",
      "html": "toori ni.... expreses the idea that something takes place in the same way as something... or it could be negative also.. means doesn't take place..",
      "credits_raw": "prachi_saurabh",
      "content_sha256": "76e264df1fa3192d7b8a95b5831db2f389df9a78e30e2fc93d536cb73e36086f",
      "original_created_at": null,
      "original_updated_at": null
    },
    {
      "position": 10,
      "source_id": null,
      "text": "\"expreses the idea that something takes place in the same way as something\" does not make any sense at all.",
      "html": "\"expreses the idea that something takes place in the same way as something\" does not make any sense at all.",
      "credits_raw": "bamboo4",
      "content_sha256": "3d8353653831e3f10d9a22f86ffd3e2e194fe1ad850a052c55d52df10e021819",
      "original_created_at": null,
      "original_updated_at": null
    },
    {
      "position": 11,
      "source_id": null,
      "text": "I have always thought of　\n「〜 通りに」　as ”like 〜”\n\nand \n「〜通り」as \"same way as 〜\" \n\nローマにいる間、ローマ人の通りにします｡\nwhile in rome, do like the romans do.\n\nローマにいる間、ローマ人の通りします｡\nwhile in rome, do things the way romans do.\n\nthe meaning doesn`t change much, but thinking of it like this makes translation less complicated.",
      "html": "I have always thought of　<br/>「〜 通りに」　as ”like 〜”<br/><br/>and <br/>「〜通り」as \"same way as 〜\" <br/><br/>ローマにいる間、ローマ人の通りにします｡<br/>while in rome, do like the romans do.<br/><br/>ローマにいる間、ローマ人の通りします｡<br/>while in rome, do things the way romans do.<br/><br/>the meaning doesn`t change much, but thinking of it like this makes translation less complicated.",
      "credits_raw": "tigert",
      "content_sha256": "faf378752d3fe660f09cd962a701bc833d231dc39057e8f9d4647176ca8964d6",
      "original_created_at": null,
      "original_updated_at": null
    },
    {
      "position": 12,
      "source_id": null,
      "text": "In ex #6257, I don't understand \"卵z\". So instead of \"Checked\" I changed it to \"suspicious\"...",
      "html": "In ex #6257, I don't understand \"卵z\". So instead of \"Checked\" I changed it to \"suspicious\"...",
